  {
   "title": "Parallel resonance",
   "body": "With $R$, $L$ and $C$ in parallel, the resonant frequency is the same $f_0 = 1/(2\\pi\\sqrt{LC})$, but now $Z_p$ is **maximum** ($Z_p = R$). Driven by a current $I$, the voltage peaks at $IR$, a bandpass response with $B = f_0/Q_p$. At resonance $|I_L| = |I_C| = Q_p|I|$. Note that $Q_p$ is the reciprocal form of $Q_s$.",
   "formula": "Q_p = \\frac{R}{2\\pi f_0 L} = 2\\pi f_0 C R",
